Subject: [PATCH] synatlsmoc: register experimental Dynabook 06cb:00d4

The Dynabook G83/HS exposes the same USB endpoint layout as synatlsmoc.
Register it for controlled hardware testing. This is not a claim of working
TLS pairing, enrollment or verification: those operations remain untested.
Keep the existing firmware, public-key and TLS checks intact.

Base: vojtapl/libfprint 0c67248a5a4af188d6c1417fb348f655e80f6c8e

diff --git a/data/autosuspend.hwdb b/data/autosuspend.hwdb
--- a/data/autosuspend.hwdb
+++ b/data/autosuspend.hwdb
@@ -274,6 +274,7 @@ ID_PERSIST=0
 usb:v06CBp00BE*
 usb:v06CBp00C9*
 usb:v06CBp00D1*
+usb:v06CBp00D4*
 usb:v06CBp00D6*
 usb:v06CBp00D8*
 usb:v06CBp00E7*
diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/synatlsmoc/synatlsmoc.c b/libfprint/drivers/synatlsmoc/synatlsmoc.c
--- a/libfprint/drivers/synatlsmoc/synatlsmoc.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/synatlsmoc/synatlsmoc.c
@@ -131,6 +131,8 @@ static const FpIdEntry id_table[] = {
     { .vid = SYNAPTICS_VENDOR_ID,  .pid = 0x00BE, },
     { .vid = SYNAPTICS_VENDOR_ID,  .pid = 0x00C9, },
     { .vid = SYNAPTICS_VENDOR_ID,  .pid = 0x00D1, },
+    /* Experimental: Dynabook G83/HS, hardware validation pending. */
+    { .vid = SYNAPTICS_VENDOR_ID,  .pid = 0x00D4, },
     { .vid = SYNAPTICS_VENDOR_ID,  .pid = 0x00D6,
       .driver_data = SYNATLSMOC_DRIVER_DATA_HAS_LED, },
     { .vid = SYNAPTICS_VENDOR_ID,  .pid = 0x00D8, },
